#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134759} :activity/id #uuid "cb02e51b-dee7-54a8-8f76-914d0b42e66b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050003 :topic/id #uuid "24e61144-3626-5d23-b2e6-a33ee94f32f3" :topic/math-academy-id 2151} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134759 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135088 :tutorial/content "How do we represent the double integral of a function over a non-rectangular region as a repeated integral? \n\nSpecifically, let's consider\n![](images/3a/3ac99dd8336c3a877fbf6ba63a3074a490b85c8a350adad00da423412dd60ee3.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg)  is the finite region enclosed by the lines ![](images/df/df9822243c11ec9f0fabca5cc578976d0bdea2c521b4f61964f5f3850a970504.svg), ![](images/1f/1fb9f2f73a09599931892c1dee7629975b4d851e5dd6f0d07b7c641bbf17bf54.svg), ![](images/23/238e977be23f692486c8bf68f6b40255435b3d1796cc50d260a014a8c670be7b.svg) and ![](images/b5/b5489c125683eb29c2cababe2e1b7094d6a16b89d09970c42af649df70d045e4.svg) as shown below.\n\n![](images/af/af0a1a74df8aec0d5189dc2402fc1840c25d4cd94d8861fa06110cae7b449843.png)\n\nFirst, notice that ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is a *type I* region. \nTo determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/39/39629b33e25aed05bf9a5ca36180f984e7ff8f863c6966d47f60483d672a8af4.png)\n\nSo, the region ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) can be defined as \n\n![](images/78/78cf2ea7f960497f7cc9beea602bf6ca0e82b74491f9f56cce76130d965d4a64.svg)\n\nNow, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n![](images/3c/3c423b0d423203621ab89258a6fff4cea190279b4dcc7170c8a7070bf1f85e24.svg)\n\nAnd that's our answer! Notice that, when we have a type I region, \n\n- the limits for ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) are functions of ![](images/5a/5aac2c81021f3f9e468e7840c5f95ece35c10b894bdae19ec1d247bdeb47ac6f.svg)\n\n- the limits for ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) are constants, and\n\n- we integrate over the variable ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) before integrating over the variable ![](images/cf/cff7b257e3c71ec70dc7cd273bdd1cced4254993a43cffbfc338460c21bc7319.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "7c641021-bc5e-5b05-8a23-b198735ee5a3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4261 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4a5c014d-2a5f-5ef2-b451-9d6636c3241e" :step/math-academy-id 25905 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134760}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134760 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133839 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133654 :question/id #uuid "51467bae-f181-53ba-adf2-1218dc16275f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7024"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e891363-fea2-5de4-9bbb-67fddb077200" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050828}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134314} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134523} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348432} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351297} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380928} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380942}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Given"} :step/id #uuid "3edf61a9-ab06-533a-ad5f-906f95245bb3" :step/math-academy-id 25906 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133840 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133655 :question/id #uuid "7f443df5-1c26-5af4-9541-e83522126197" :question/math-academy-id "e-7025"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853b2770-5057-50aa-9c15-7426cf4cc6a4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134313} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134326} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326881} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326888} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326889} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351299} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380949} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380956} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382482} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394160}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Not Given"} :step/id #uuid "621aac0e-49f3-510c-b684-d0f438398280" :step/math-academy-id 25907 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134762}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134762 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135089 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we want to evaluate the repeated integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{x}^{2x} (x-2y) \\ \\mathrm{d}  y \\ \\mathrm{d}  x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the domain of integration is a type I region. \n\nTo compute this integral, we must bear the following important points in mind.\n\n- We start with the inner integral, as usual.\n\n- When integrating with respect to $y,$ we treat $x$ as though it were a constant.\n\n- The limits of integration for the inner integral are functions of $x.$ Once again, we treat $x$ as though it were a constant and substitute the integration limits as usual. After this step, there should be no more $y$'s in our integral.\n\n- Finally, we compute the outer integral.\n\nLet's apply these steps to solve the given problem.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x}^{2x}(x-2y)\\text{ }dy]\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[xy-{y}^{2}]_{x}^{2x}\\text{ }dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[x\\cdot (2x)-{(2x)}^{2}]-[x\\cdot (x)-(x)^{2}]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}]-[{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,dx & =-2{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3698e7e3-4bc2-5db0-96b5-172131284b4a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4262 :tutorial/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals With Variable Limits"} :step/id #uuid "59bc86e8-4dae-564b-ab2b-c8ac5309d3be" :step/math-academy-id 25908 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134763}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134763 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133841 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133656 :question/id #uuid "b151be22-91a1-5303-b86d-4f9ba748f000" :question/math-academy-id "e-7026"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a28c4320-e2dd-5195-81ac-b910c2328691" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050213}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134200} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134526} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268859} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351300} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382085} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382489}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Repeated Integral Defined Over a Type I Region"} :step/id #uuid "9095d8fd-3ce2-5af6-bda4-4a49a820addf" :step/math-academy-id 25909 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134764}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134764 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133842 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133657 :question/id #uuid "24dd94c8-2821-5614-9ccf-43c3656267f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-7027"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69f6b2a7-7a3a-5c2c-90db-5aa321784048" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134199} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134201} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323959} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351301} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351302} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351375} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351376} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351377} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380977} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380984} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382065}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Double Integral Defined Over a Type I Region"} :step/id #uuid "bb2a0a7b-340c-53a3-a510-9a559cc6d898" :step/math-academy-id 25911}] :activity/title "Double Integrals Over Type I Regions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134026}]}
